# Logged-in tour of the Treechat app on a real phone: feed, tabs, posts,
# search, notifications, sidebar, channels. Read-only: never posts, replies,
# joins or upvalues (use a test account with no sats). The account comes from
# the environment (or ./.env): TREECHAT_EMAIL, TREECHAT_PASSWORD.
#   jevb run examples/tour-treechat-app-loggedin.jevb --device "pixel 9" --app treechat.apk --pace agent

open
act? dismiss the notifications permission prompt without allowing
check is this a login page?
type the email field => ${TREECHAT_EMAIL}
type the password field => ${TREECHAT_PASSWORD}
press HideKeyboard
act log in
refute is an error or "wrong password" message shown?
check is the user logged in?

# The app reopens wherever this account last was (a Channels page, say):
# start from the home feed.
act go to the Home feed with the house icon in the bottom bar
check is the home feed with posts shown?

# The feed
scroll 1500
check are posts shown?
scroll -1500
act? switch the feed to Hot
check are posts shown?
act? switch the feed back to Now
act? switch to the Following tab
act? switch back to the Public tab

# Open a post and come back
act open the first post in the feed by tapping its text
check is a single post or conversation thread shown?
press Back
check is the home feed shown?
scroll 1200
act open a post by tapping its text
check is a single post or conversation thread shown?
scroll 800
press Back

# Search
act open search
type the search field => ordinals
press Enter
check are search results shown?
press Back

# Notifications
act open notifications
check are notifications shown?
press Back

# Sidebar: channels, memes, home
act open the sidebar menu
act open the Channels page
check is a list of channels shown?
act open the first channel in the list
check is a channel's stream of posts shown?
scroll 1200
press Back
act open the sidebar menu
act? open Memes
check is a page of memes shown?
act open the sidebar menu
act go to Home
check is the home feed shown?
